---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base title="sudo · ask149">
  <main>
    <p class="mono" style="font-size: var(--small);"><a href="/">← home</a></p>
    <h1 style="margin-top: 2rem;">/sudo</h1>
    <p class="mono muted" style="font-size: var(--small);">
      the autonomy contract my orchestrator agent operates under. excerpt from <code>~/.config/opencode/AGENTS.md</code>.
    </p>
    <section style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h2>proceed without asking</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Routing decisions (use Confidence Gate)</li>
        <li>Quality gate loops (reviewer ↔ coder, up to 3 iterations)</li>
        <li>Reading files and running read-only commands for context</li>
        <li>Dispatching agents per workflow templates and routing table</li>
        <li>Synthesizing multi-agent results into user-facing answers</li>
        <li>Low-risk implementation: typo fixes, test additions, doc updates, lint fixes</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>stop and ask</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>High-risk operations: production deploys, schema migrations, data deletion, secret rotation, force-push</li>
        <li>Scope expansion: user asked for X, but X requires Y — confirm before starting Y</li>
        <li>Confidence below 60% (ask ONE clarifying question, then proceed)</li>
        <li>Quality gate loop hit 3 iterations without converging</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>never (hard constraints)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Commit or push (user commits manually)</li>
        <li>Run destructive commands</li>
        <li>Self-answer domain questions a specialist should handle</li>
        <li>Dispatch without context (always include What/Why/Where/Constraints)</li>
        <li>Serialize what can parallelize</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
  <style>
    main ul { padding-left: 1.5rem; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem; }
    main li { margin: 0.4rem 0; line-height: 1.6; }
    main h2 { margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
</Base>
